ween lan-a (vtnet1/opt1, 10.60.10.0/24, toward node2) and lan-b (vtnet2/opt2, 10.60.20.0/24, toward node3). Added a logged pf block rule for TCP/23 on both opt1 and opt2 (other traffic still passes), verified a telnet-style attempt from node2 to node3 is refused and logged on node1's filter log, then restarted all three nodes one at a time and re-verified the block+log behavior and network state persisted after each restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Discovered actual topology: node1 (OPNsense/FreeBSD) has vtnet0 (shared mgmt network), vtnet1 (link to node2), vtnet2 (link to node3); node2/node3 (Ubuntu 16.04) each have ens2 (mgmt) and ens7 (lan link)\",\"Assigned OPNsense interfaces opt1=lan-a (10.60.10.1/24 on vtnet1) and opt2=lan-b (10.60.20.1/24 on vtnet2) via config.xml edit + configctl interface reconfigure\",\"Added pf filter rules per interface: block+log TCP port 23 (quick), then pass-all for other traffic; applied via configctl filter reload; fixed a duplicate-port XML bug found via the PHP filter-compile error\",\"Statically configured node2 ens7=10.60.10.2/24 and node3 ens7=10.60.20.2/24 persistently via /etc/network/interfaces.d/*.cfg, with cross-LAN static routes added the same way\",\"Verified cross-LAN ping works (pass rule) and a TCP/23 connection from node2 to node3 times out (blocked)\",\"Located and displayed the OPNsense filter log entry on node1 (/var/log/filter/filter_20260905.log) showing block,in on vtnet1 from 10.60.10.2 (node2) to 10.60.20.2 port 23\",\"Captured pre-restart boot markers (FreeBSD kern.boottime; Linux /proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id) and health evidence for all 3 nodes\",\"Restarted node1, node2, node3 sequentially (one at a time) using native reboot (shutdown -r now), polled each until exec was available again, and confirmed each node's boot marker changed\",\"Post-restart, re-verified on all nodes: interface IPs/routes persisted, pf rules present, forwarding enabled, cross-LAN ping still works, and a repeat telnet attempt from node2 to node3:23 was again blocked and logged on node1\",\"Cleaned up temporary nc listener on node3 and scratch files on node1\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"node1 routes between lan-a and lan-b\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8338e3e161344195\",\"cmd-b9d5c9a511f7498d\",\"cmd-c521cfd7f8cd46c9\",\"cmd-2f84dd8591b0499e\"],\"summary\":\"node1's vtnet1/vtnet2 identified as links to node2/node3 respectively; configured as opt1=lan-a/opt2=lan-b; cross-LAN ping from node2 (10.60.10.2) to node3 (10.60.20.2) succeeds through node1.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Refuse TCP port 23 between lan-a and lan-b\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-045714a52c834186\",\"cmd-8f2d48432fde4a87\",\"cmd-0817c456bbbd4c1d\"],\"summary\":\"pf ruleset shows block-quick-log rules for tcp port 23 on vtnet1 and vtnet2; live telnet-style (nc) connection attempts from node2 to node3:23 time out both before and after restart.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Record every refused attempt in a log on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-4a79016d2f594b39\",\"cmd-cc35cfac14b94816\"],\"summary\":\"node1's /var/log/filter/filter_20260905.log contains block,in entries on vtnet1 tagged with the block rule's label, for every SYN retry from 10.60.10.2 to 10.60.20.2:23, both pre- and post-restart.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Show a log entry produced by an attempt made from node2\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-4a79016d2f594b39\"],\"summary\":\"Filter log line: block,in on vtnet1 from 10.60.10.2 (node2) to 10.60.20.2 port 23 -- directly attributable to node2's nc connection attempt.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Mandatory restart evidence - node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-805c3a00ff114c2d\",\"cmd-0dbff2927c9a4a6a\",\"cmd-4cb4d931b0ec4c26\",\"cmd-01afde9806404ff9\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline kern.boottime captured (1788629867); reboot acknowledged; exec available again; new kern.boottime (1788630221) proves restart; interfaces, pf rules, and forwarding all recovered.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Mandatory restart evidence - node2\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f29a1619122f4b66\",